{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA confirmed on current origin/main (23591dc0)\n\n**Proven mechanism.** `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:record_mcp_backoff_failure()` (now ~L668) unconditionally calls `err deploy_failed \"component=mcp ...\"`, and `err()` (~L239) emits an `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR {...}` marker. It is invoked on the TWO documented-routine backoff paths:\n- low-memory abort (~L898-899): `marker AUTODEPLOY_MCP_MEM_ABORT ...; record_mcp_backoff_failure; exit 1`\n- port-exhausted retire-cap (~L907-908): `marker AUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP ...; record_mcp_backoff_failure; exit 1`\n\n`observability.sh` counts `^AUTODEPLOY_ERROR \\{` markers into `rebar/host:deploy_errors` (~L232/242) and explicitly documents (~L284-291, L355) that the retire-cap/mem-abort tokens are \"each kept out of AUTODEPLOY_ERROR so a routine retire-cap / memory abort never inflates deploy_errors\" — the sustained case has its own `mcp_retire_cap` / `mcp_mem_abort` alarms. The code contradicts its own contract, false-paging `rebar-autodeploy-errors`.\n\n**Discriminating proof (runtime).** New test `test_port_exhausted_routine_backoff_does_not_inflate_deploy_errors` driving the real script with both blue/green ports held shows the journal emitting BOTH markers for one event:\n```\nAUTODEPLOY_MCP_RETIRE_CAP {\"reason\":\"port-exhausted\", ...}\nAUTODEPLOY_ERROR {\"reason\":\"deploy_failed\",\"detail\":\"component=mcp ... fail#1 backoff=60s\"}\n```\nThe retire-cap marker (liveness anchor) fires AND deploy_failed fires — reproducing the live 2026-08-30 incident. Genuine-failure paths (mcp-unhealthy etc., ~L760-991) are unaffected and still emit `deploy_failed` (existing `test_mcp_failure_keeps_the_deploy_failed_metric_and_names_the_component`).\n\n**Classification: `defect`** — violates the cited authoritative contract in observability.sh (same file family, standing intent). Not a design decision.\n\n**Defect origin (caused_by): `6964-40bb-46c9-48a7`** (panicky-sylphish-foxterrier, \"infra: add mcp blue-green autodeploy target\", commit `2a0a4b19f2ab`, 2026-08-25). That single commit introduced BOTH the observability.sh \"kept out of deploy_errors\" contract AND the autodeploy.sh routine paths that call the deploy_failed-emitting recorder (`record_backoff_failure` then, `err deploy_failed` inside) — an internally-inconsistent plan. `d2eed2c4e8d7` (\"per-component deploy state\") only renamed the recorder to `record_mcp_backoff_failure` on those lines; it is a carrier, not the origin. Close class: **plan_defect**.\n\n**Fix (Phase 2):** factor the backoff-timer bookkeeping (write `$MCP_BACKOFF_FILE` + prune) out of the `err deploy_failed` emission via a `schedule_mcp_backoff` helper; add a `record_mcp_routine_backoff` variant (schedule + log, no `err`) for the two routine paths. Genuine-failure paths keep calling `record_mcp_backoff_failure` (schedule + `err deploy_failed`). Throttle (AC #4) preserved on all paths."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788071613765643218,"uuid":"bb3b5012-b92f-49b7-84cd-43ecbdecb3b7"}